<description><![CDATA[<video controls><source src="" poster="https://www.instagram.com/p/DgH6-uwo7ia/media?size=l" type="video/mp4"><img src="https://www.instagram.com/p/DgH6-uwo7ia/media?size=l" alt=""></video><br><br>Recipe ⬇️ (470 Cals | ~37g Protein | ~7.8g Fibre)<br />
<br />
🌾 30g besan<br />
💧 Water, as needed<br />
🧂 Salt, to taste<br />
🌶️ Red chilli powder, to taste<br />
⚫ Black pepper, to taste<br />
🌿 Jeera powder, to taste<br />
🥬 Chopped spinach<br />
🫓 1 roti or tortilla<br />
🥬 Lettuce leaves<br />
🧀 1 cheese slice<br />
🍅 2 tomato slices<br />
🥣 80g high-protein, low-fat paneer, crumbled<br />
🌶️ 1 tsp chilli oil<br />
🥫 Sauce or chutney, for serving (optional)<br />
<br />
👨🏻&zwj;🍳 How to Make<br />
<br />
1. Mix besan, salt, red chilli powder, black pepper, jeera powder and water to make a smooth, flowing batter slightly thinner than dosa batter.<br />
2. Pour the batter onto a hot tawa and spread it into a thin cheela. Sprinkle chopped spinach on top while its wet.<br />
3. Place a roti or tortilla over the spinach after it slightly cooks, pressing gently. Let it cook, then flip and lightly toast the roti side without making it too crispy.<br />
4. Flip again so the roti side faces up. Add lettuce, a cheese slice, tomato slices and crumbled high-protein paneer mixed with chilli oil.<br />
5. Make one cut from the bottom edge towards the centre, creating a quarter-fold opening. Fold the wrap section by section as shown in the video.<br />
6. Cut the folded wrap in half and enjoy with your favourite sauce or chutney!<br />
<br />
