<description><![CDATA[<video controls><source src="" poster="https://www.instagram.com/p/DgCOL6VonIT/media?size=l" type="video/mp4"><img src="https://www.instagram.com/p/DgCOL6VonIT/media?size=l" alt=""></video><br><br>500+ mad tasty but high protein and low calorie recipes on my page that will make you fall in love with healthy meals ❤️ Toh bass follow karlo?🥰<br />
<br />
Recipe ⬇️ (417 Cals | ~30g Protein | 7-8 Fibre)<br />
<br />
🌶️ 1 tsp chilli oil<br />
🧄 3&ndash;4 garlic cloves, chopped<br />
🧅 1 medium onion, finely chopped<br />
🥣 220g silken tofu<br />
🥛 150ml unsweetened soy milk<br />
🥜 &frac12; tbsp unsweetened peanut butter<br />
🧂 Salt, to taste<br />
🍯 Zero-calorie sweetener, to taste<br />
🥢 1 tbsp soy sauce<br />
🌶️ 1 tsp red chilli powder<br />
💧 Water, as needed<br />
🍜 &frac34; pack shirataki noodles<br />
🥜 1 tsp roasted crushed peanuts (optional)<br />
🌱 Chopped spring onions, for garnish<br />
🍋 Juice of &frac12; lemon<br />
<br />
👨🏻&zwj;🍳 How to Make<br />
<br />
1. Heat chilli oil in a pan. Add chopped garlic and finely chopped onion, then saut&eacute; until softened.<br />
2. Blend silken tofu, soy milk and a little salt until completely smooth and creamy.<br />
3. Add peanut butter to the saut&eacute;ed garlic and onion. Mix well, then pour in the tofu mixture and cook for 2&ndash;3 minutes.<br />
4. Add salt, zero-calorie sweetener, soy sauce and red chilli powder. Mix well and adjust the consistency with a little water.<br />
5. Add shirataki noodles, mix until well coated and cook for another 3&ndash;4 minutes.<br />
6. Transfer to a bowl. Top with optional roasted crushed peanuts, chopped spring onions and a squeeze of lemon juice. Enjoy!<br />
